[104.305957, "o", "'''+s[pos:]; p.write_text(s)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> p=Path('tests/test_delta.py'); s=p.read_text().replace('Pages(page(\"first\", [item(1, \"A\")])) )', 'Pages(page(\"first\", [item(1, \"A\")])))'); p.write_text(s)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> p=Path('README.md'); s=p.read_text(); s+='''\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Delta checkpoints and existing catalogs\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Sync applies both upserts and tombstones in sequence order, including across\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> empty sequence windows. Each page and its opaque `feed_cursor` commit together;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> if a later page fails, rerunning resumes after the last committed page. An\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> up-to-date run makes one request at that cursor to check for new changes. An\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> invalid/old-epoch cursor is reported as an error, not silently reset.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Existing append-only catalogs are migrated to a unique SKU index, retaining the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> highest `feed_seq` per SKU (latest inserted row bre"]
[104.306064, "o", "aks ties). Feed records are\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> then updated in place. Prices are parsed as exact decimal cents.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Supplier notices are logged. A `notice_ack_required` response is retried at the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> same cursor with the documented acknowledgement header. Notice text does not\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> change local pricing policy: sync never prunes or modifies `price_overrides`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Expired and future overrides are ignored when computing effective prices;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> historical rows remain available unless an operator explicitly runs\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `overrides prune-expired`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> '''; p.write_text(s)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> PY\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
